vo_frame_output.c: register a VideoToolbox decode device, and pack
software frames into display-grade buffers.

Two defects, one symptom (device testing, 2026-11-24: playback runs
and audio plays, but the picture is black):

1. preinit() never published a decode device.  A non-copying hwdec
   can only take its device from the VO's hwdec_devs
   (vd_lavc.c: hwdec_create_dev() queries
   hwdec_devices_get_by_imgfmt_and_type() and gives up with "Could
   not create device" when no ctx matches), so the player's
   hwdec=videotoolbox request could never initialise and every
   stream silently fell back to software decoding — the frame
   pipeline never once took the zero-copy CVPixelBuffer path the
   original uses.  Upstream's ra_hwdec_videotoolbox cannot fill the
   gap: only the gpu backends load it, and its init refuses to run
   without a GL or libplacebo interop (hwdec_vt.c), both disabled
   here by design.  preinit() therefore does what that driver's
   init does after its interop exists — av_hwdevice_ctx_create(
   AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_VIDEOTOOLBOX) + hwdec_devices_add() — the same
   shape as vo_mediacodec_embed's preinit.  uninit() removes the
   ctx and destroys the device list (hwdec_devices_destroy asserts
   both).

2. The software fallback that defect 1 made permanent packs frames
   into bare CVPixelBuffers: created with NULL attributes (backing
   store unspecified — no IOSurface properties, no Metal
   compatibility) and with no colour attachments, so the format
   description the host builds from the buffer carries no primaries
   / transfer / YCbCr matrix at all.  VideoToolbox buffers carry
   all of this natively.  fo_pack_image() now creates its buffers
   with IOSurface + Metal-compatibility attributes, and a new
   fo_attach_color() copies the colour description from the frame's
   mp_image_params (params.color.primaries / .transfer,
   params.repr.sys) onto the packed buffer, so the retained
   software path produces the same class of buffer the hardware
   path does.

diff --git a/video/out/vo_frame_output.c b/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
index 07dd178..57a06c5 100644
